# Product Phase 6F — Live Paper Validation

## What Phase 6F does

Phase 6F validates the completed Phase 6A-6E historical-research pipeline
against **real / near-live Yahoo market data during the live market session**,
using **paper trading only**. It answers:

> "When the system sees a current market state, what did historical research
> say about similar setups, and how does that historical expectation compare
> with the actual subsequent paper-trading outcome?"

```
LIVE / NEAR-LIVE DATA (existing provider; COMPLETED candles only)
    |
existing DashboardAnalysisService.analyze     (authoritative decision)
    |
existing Phase 6E historical evidence context (attached to the view)
    |
existing PaperTradingOperations.run_once      (track + create + persist)
    |
LiveValidationObservation per instrument      (Phase 6F — this layer)
    |
LiveValidationStore (dedicated persistence; REFERENCES research ids +
    paper-trade ids — never duplicates the heavy records)
    |
historical-vs-actual comparison report (descriptive only)
```

> Historical evidence is observational research context. It does not predict
> future returns, guarantee profitability, or override the authoritative
> decision engine.

## Architecture

Phase 6F is a THIN ORCHESTRATION layer. It implements NO new market analysis,
NO decision logic, NO geometry, NO position sizing, NO outcome engine, NO
prediction / probability, NO ML / LLM, NO broker connectivity and NO
BUY/SELL/ENTER/EXIT/HOLD recommendation. Every component is REUSED:

* **Provider + completed-candle boundary** — the existing Product Phase 1
  provider abstraction (`YahooDataProvider` live / `FixtureDataProvider`
  deterministic). The forming candle NEVER enters the analysis, the decision
  or the outcome.
* **Decision** — the existing Sprint 11S classification
  (REJECTED / WATCH / QUALIFIED / PREFERRED) is AUTHORITATIVE and reused
  VERBATIM — never renamed to BUY/SELL, never upgraded / downgraded, never
  overridden by historical evidence.
* **Historical evidence** — read from the existing
  `DashboardTradeView.historical_context` attachment (Phase 6E
  `HistoricalEvidenceLookupEngine` over the persisted Phase 6D
  `SetupResearchStore`). Phase 6F NEVER re-runs the Phase 6D research and
  NEVER performs a second lookup with different semantics.
* **Paper trading** — paper trades are created / tracked / persisted
  EXCLUSIVELY through the existing `PaperTradingOperations` cycle (the same
  READY_FOR_REVIEW eligibility gate, duplicate prevention and lifecycle).
  Phase 6F NEVER creates a paper trade itself.
* **Outcomes** — read from the existing paper-trade lifecycle records. No
  second outcome engine; no outcome is fabricated.

