## Lifecycle

One `run_once()` validation cycle:

1. Resolve the instrument watchlist from the EXISTING configured universe
   mechanism (`service.available_instruments()`); nothing is hard-coded.
2. Run the EXISTING `PaperTradingOperations.run_once` (tracks + creates
   paper trades through the authoritative eligibility gate; persists them
   through the existing `PaperTradeStore`).
3. For each instrument (sorted, failure-isolated): run the existing analysis
   (completed candles only), read the attached Phase 6E historical evidence
   context, link any paper trade the operations cycle created / tracked for
   that instrument, and build a `LiveValidationObservation`.
4. Persist each observation IDEMPOTENTLY (deterministic `lval-...` id;
   unchanged observations are not re-written; outcome-advancing updates bump
   `revision` + append history).
5. Refresh previously-recorded OPEN observations whose referenced paper
   trade advanced (the historical-vs-actual comparison completes honestly
   when the actual outcome arrives — never fabricated earlier).

## Validation states (non-predictive)

`OBSERVED` — current state + evidence recorded; no paper trade referenced.
`PAPER_TRADE_CREATED` — an eligible opportunity created a paper trade this
cycle through the existing operations layer.
`PAPER_TRADE_ACTIVE` — the referenced paper trade is still non-terminal.
`COMPLETED` — the referenced paper trade reached a terminal state; the actual
outcome is recorded (realized R only when the existing engine provides it).
`NO_OPPORTUNITY` — no opportunity / no usable decision (a valid observation).
`REJECTED` — the authoritative decision was REJECTED (a valid observation).
`NOT_READY` — the validation layer is not initialized (no store).
`ERROR` — the instrument failed this cycle (provider / analysis / persistence
failure), recorded explicitly.

There are NO probabilistic prediction states. A rejected or no-opportunity
observation is still a valid validation observation.

## Point-in-time rules

At evaluation time `T`:

```
current setup:      setup candles <= T ; context candles < T
historical research: occurrence < T AND outcome already resolved at T
paper-trade outcome: resolves strictly AFTER the evaluation timestamp
```

* Only completed candles are used for analysis and outcome evaluation; the
  forming candle never enters the intelligence or decision engine.
* `run_once()` accepts NO `future` / `future_candles` / `lookahead`
  parameter.
* The Sprint 11W `OutcomeEvaluator` is NEVER invoked by the validation layer
  (paper-trade touch logic lives in the existing paper-trading engine).
* The historical pipeline is NEVER re-run.
* A fixed-T observation is unaffected by appending future candles
  (regression-tested).

## Persistence

* JSON only, deterministic (sorted keys), schema-versioned
  (`LIVE_VALIDATION_SCHEMA_VERSION = 1`, checked BEFORE model
  reconstruction).
* One document per observation (`<directory>/<validation_id>.validation`).
  The `.validation` suffix (intentionally NOT `.json`) prevents polluting
  the paper-trade store / experiment registry / research store listings in a
  shared directory.
* Atomic writes (same-dir temp + flush + fsync best-effort + `os.replace`).
* Safe-id validation (path-traversal proof); corruption detection via typed
  errors (`LiveValidationIntegrityError`); filename-id integrity checks.
* Append/history semantics: one journal line per persisted revision
  (`<validation_id>.validation.history.jsonl`); the main file holds the
  latest revision.
* Idempotent: the same setup at the same `T` resolves to the same
  deterministic `lval-...` id; re-running a cycle against the same completed
  candle creates no duplicate observation and no duplicate paper trade.
* The existing `PaperTradeStore` schema is NOT modified — observations
  REFERENCE paper-trade ids and Phase 6D research ids (provenance retained;
  heavy records never duplicated).

## Historical-vs-live comparison

`LiveValidationFormatter.format_cycle(result)` renders, per instrument:
Instrument, Evaluation time, Current decision, Current actionability,
Historical evidence status, Historical evidence strength, Historical sample
size, Historical statistics (win rate / average realized R / profit factor),
Paper trade created?, Paper trade outcome, Realized result / R, Validation
status.

The comparison is DESCRIPTIVE: it never claims historical evidence predicts
the future, never computes a predictive probability, and never creates a new
trading score. The three concerns (current decision / historical evidence /
actual paper-trade outcome) are presented separately — never merged.

## Failure handling (failure isolation)

One instrument failing never aborts the cycle. Provider failure, stale data,
historical research unavailable, no historical match, rejected decision, no
opportunity, incomplete geometry, paper-trade persistence failure and
unavailable outcome are all recorded EXPLICITLY (status + warnings + cycle
errors) — never silently converted into a successful validation.

## Scheduler integration

Phase 6F exposes a single explicit `LivePaperValidation.run_once()` API and
the operator CLI `scripts/run_live_paper_validation.py`. The EXISTING
market-session scheduler / keep-awake launcher
(`scripts/windows/run_paper_trading_cycle.bat` + `Install-PaperTradingTask.ps1`)
can invoke this entry point on the same cadence as the existing paper-trading
cycle — NO second scheduler is created, and the existing 09:15-16:00 session
behavior, keep-awake process, completed-candle handling, Yahoo provider and
paper-trading-only limitation are preserved unchanged. The CLI defaults
`DASHBOARD_PROVIDER` to `yahoo` without overwriting an explicit value.

## Multi-instrument operation

The instrument universe is resolved through the EXISTING configurable
universe / watchlist mechanism (`engine.config.universe` /
`dashboard.watchlist` / `service.available_instruments()`); the current
configured universe contains the NIFTY 50 ∪ SENSEX coverage. Nothing is
hard-coded in the validation layer, and provider code is not modified to
define the universe.

## Paper-trading-only limitation

This system performs paper trading only. No real orders are placed. There is
NO broker API, NO order execution, NO position management at a broker and NO
automatic financial transaction anywhere in Phase 6F.

## Interpretation limitations

* Historical evidence is observational research context. It does not predict
  future returns, guarantee profitability, or override the authoritative
  decision engine.
* Paper-trade results never rewrite the original system decision; a
  paper-trade outcome is a SEPARATE concern from the authoritative decision
  classification.
* The validation observation references persisted research + paper-trade
  records; it is an audit view, not a second source of intelligence.
* The comparison is descriptive. A favorable historical statistic does NOT
  imply the current paper trade will succeed, and an unfavorable one does
  NOT imply it will fail.
* The existing paper-trade lifecycle semantics are inherited unchanged
  (including mark-to-close EXPIRED at the end of the supplied completed
  candle window and BOTH_TOUCHED ambiguity, where realized R is never
  fabricated).
